{"title":"1965 AHSME Problems/Problem 32","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Problem\">Problem</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1965_AHSME_Problems/Problem_32&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Problem\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>An article costing <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> dollars is sold for \\$100 at a loss of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> percent of the selling price. \nIt is then resold at a profit of <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> percent of the new selling price <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/3/bf344aa376979a8a81e8784f92fcb2381897ba65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S&#39;$\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" />. \nIf the difference between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/3/bf344aa376979a8a81e8784f92fcb2381897ba65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S&#39;$\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/b/e/8be0c5f0727519503a8ca0f6a602a59be0fe9e42.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$1\\frac {1}{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" /> dollars, then <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" /> is: \n</p><p><img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/f/3/6/f3614908fa7eaa253cbf6b35197b06e8cf22e664.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\textbf{(A)}\\ \\text{undetermined} \\qquad  \\textbf{(B) }\\ \\frac {80}{9} \\qquad  \\textbf{(C) }\\ 10 \\qquad  \\textbf{(D) }\\ \\frac{95}{9}\\qquad \\textbf{(E) }\\ \\frac{100}{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"521\" height=\"37\" />  \n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Solution\">Solution</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1965_AHSME_Problems/Problem_32&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Solution\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<p>The magnitude of the loss after the first sale is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/4/1/1415485ed0dfedd75f706a4d5cf6c6fc6ab949af.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C-100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"66\" height=\"16\" />, which equals <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />% of the selling price, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/c/6/dc6a1da7f18069a90481296d18af7ca979fe3854.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\$100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"35\" height=\"14\" />. Thus, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/1/c/8/1c8c51da01f773045dd9497b3dbc4b81cb6e9d76.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C-100=100*\\frac{x}{100}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"166\" height=\"34\" />, and so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/8/a/5/8a545bba994e5cb3c7a082cbd46b7783be49df8b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C=x+100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"100\" height=\"16\" />. The profit made after the second sale, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/d/e/5/de54e67d890934ac03cc61d27b383f95c54a12ce.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S&#39;-100$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"68\" height=\"17\" />, is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/2/6/e/26eeb5258ca5099acf8fe96b2a1049c48c89a5e6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"12\" height=\"10\" />% of the new selling price, and this quantity is represented by <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/3/5/a/35a56dc94acf246aa7248de147f0f82a6dde2cf6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S&#39;*\\frac{x}{100}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"67\" height=\"34\" />. Equating these two expressions, we see that <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/0/3/c03ae16d64a0cfa08283e1becd07a985f615d026.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S&#39;-100=S&#39;*\\frac{x}{100}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -13px\" width=\"158\" height=\"34\" />, and so <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/7/d/47dc239d67264b0501b8b9f0aa9d5542b628218d.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S&#39;=\\frac{10,000}{100-x}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -15px\" width=\"107\" height=\"40\" />. Because we know that the difference between <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/b/f/3/bf344aa376979a8a81e8784f92fcb2381897ba65.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$S&#39;$\" width=\"15\" height=\"14\" /> and <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/c/3/3/c3355896da590fc491a10150a50416687626d7cc.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$C$\" style=\"vertical-align: -1px\" width=\"16\" height=\"14\" /> is <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/6/7/1/6717255cb76cb21041a9c983b8ebd7b8fe68728b.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\frac{10}{9}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -12px\" width=\"20\" height=\"37\" />, we can solve the following equation:\n\\begin{align*} \\\\\n\\frac{10,000}{100-x}-(x+100)&amp;=\\frac{10}{9} \\\\\n10,000-(100+x)(100-x)&amp;=\\frac{10}{9}(100-x) \\\\\n10,000-(10,000-x^2)&amp;=\\frac{1000}{9}-\\frac{10}{9}x \\\\\nx^2+\\frac{10}{9}x-\\frac{1000}{9}&amp;=0 \\\\\n9x^2+10x-1000&amp;=0 \\\\\n(9x+100)(x-10)&amp;=0 \\\\\n\\end{align*}\nBecause <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/4/4/d/44df9cb6ce6f056c64c197a004b64fc4dd3a5aa5.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x \\geq 0$\" style=\"vertical-align: -2px\" width=\"43\" height=\"15\" />, <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/e/c/1/ec186fd1809357d1f530bee2334ceb59d405b4f6.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$x=10$\" style=\"vertical-align: 0px\" width=\"52\" height=\"13\" />, and so we choose answer <img src=\"//latex.artofproblemsolving.com/9/5/a/95a37e2c613248cd21b3266be23fe9b0b6e1ac11.png\" class=\"latex\" alt=\"$\\boxed{\\textbf{(C) }10}$\" style=\"vertical-align: -11px\" width=\"66\" height=\"30\" />.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1965_AHSME_Problems/Problem_32&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<table class=\"wikitable\" style=\"margin:0.5em auto; font-size:95%; border:1px solid black; width:80%;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<td style=\"background:#ccf;text-align:center;\" colspan=\"3\"><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1965_AHSME\" title=\"1965 AHSME\">1965 AHSC</a></b> (<b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1965_AHSME_Problems\" title=\"1965 AHSME Problems\">Problems</a></b> • <b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1965_AHSME_Answer_Key\" title=\"1965 AHSME Answer Key\">Answer Key</a></b> • <a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"http://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/resources.php?c=182&amp;cid=44&amp;year=1965\">Resources</a>)\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Preceded&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1965_AHSME_Problems/Problem_31\" title=\"1965 AHSME Problems/Problem 31\">Problem 31</a></b>\n</td>\n<td width=\"50%\" align=\"center\" rowspan=\"1\">Followed&#160;by<br /><b><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1965_AHSME_Problems/Pro